---
import Layout from '../layouts/StandardLayout.astro';
import { resources } from '../data/orbit/resources';
---
<Layout title="Resources & schemas"><section class="page wide"><p class="pathbar">~/orbit/schemas</p><p class="eyebrow">ORBIT RESOURCES &amp; SCHEMAS · v0.1 DRAFT</p><h1>Machine-readable contracts.</h1><p class="lede">Four core portable record types define the ORBIT planning and reconciliation model.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="#resource-index">Browse resources</a><a class="text-link" href="/examples/plan/customer-sso">View the complete example →</a></div>

<section class="editorial" id="resource-model"><p class="section-label">RESOURCE MODEL</p><h2>Records relate by reference.</h2><pre class="code boundary-code resource-graph">                        ┌──────────────┐
                        │     Plan     │
                        │ durable      │
                        │ intent       │
                        └──────┬───────┘
                               │
                     planId + revision
                               │
                               ▼
┌───────────────────┐   ┌──────────────────┐
│ ProjectSnapshot   │   │  Reconciliation  │
│ observed state    │   │ assessment       │
└─────────┬─────────┘   └────────┬─────────┘
          │                       │
          │ projectSnapshotId     │ justifies
          └───────────────▶───────┘
                                  │
                                  ▼
                         ┌──────────────────┐
                         │ ExecutionSlice   │
                         │ bounded work     │
                         └──────────────────┘</pre><div class="split resource-relationship-grid"><div><p class="section-label">REFERENCE SEMANTICS</p><p><strong>Reconciliation</strong> references a Plan and Plan revision, a ProjectSnapshot, and canonical Acceptance Criteria.</p><p><strong>ExecutionSlice</strong> references a Plan and Plan revision, the Reconciliation that justified it, an Outcome, contributing Acceptance Criteria, and relevant repository provenance.</p></div><pre class="code boundary-code">Project
  └── 1..N Plans
        └── 1..N Outcomes

Plan
  └── 1..N Acceptance Criteria</pre></div></section>

<section class="editorial" id="resource-index"><p class="section-label">RESOURCE INDEX</p><h2>Four portable resources.</h2><div class="resource-grid">{resources.map(resource => <article class="resource-card"><p class="type-label">{resource.canonicalName}</p><h3>{resource.displayName}</h3><p>{resource.description}</p><p class="resource-meta"><b>References</b><br />{resource.references}</p><div class="resource-actions"><a href={`/schemas/${resource.key}`}>Resource guide →</a><a href={resource.schemaPath}>Raw schema ↗</a><a href={`/examples/${resource.key}/${resource.examples[1].slug}`}>Examples →</a></div></article>)}</div></section>

<section class="editorial" id="reference-table"><p class="section-label">RESOURCE REFERENCES</p><div class="table-wrap"><table class="small-table"><thead><tr><th>Resource</th><th>Purpose</th><th>References</th></tr></thead><tbody>{resources.map(resource => <tr><td><code>{resource.canonicalName}</code></td><td>{resource.description}</td><td>{resource.references}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></section>

<section class="editorial" id="complete-example"><p class="section-label">COMPLETE EXAMPLE</p><h2>Follow one outcome through the ORBIT model.</h2><pre class="code boundary-code">Plan
plan-sso @ revision 1
         │
         ▼
ProjectSnapshot
snapshot-2026-09-14
         │
         ▼
Reconciliation
reconciliation-001
         │
         ▼
ExecutionSlice
slice-001</pre><p>Each node is a complete, schema-valid resource. Open the <a href="/examples/plan/customer-sso">Plan</a>, <a href="/examples/project-snapshot/customer-platform">ProjectSnapshot</a>, <a href="/examples/reconciliation/partial-verification">Reconciliation</a>, or <a href="/examples/execution-slice/customer-sso">ExecutionSlice</a> example.</p><pre class="code boundary-code">plan-sso
├── outcome: sso
└── criterion: ac-1

snapshot-2026-09-14
└── web @ 81fee032

reconciliation-001
├── plan: plan-sso rev 1
├── snapshot: snapshot-2026-09-14
└── assesses: ac-1

slice-001
├── plan: plan-sso rev 1
├── outcome: sso
├── reconciliation: reconciliation-001
├── contributesTo: ac-1
└── web @ 81fee032</pre></section>

<section class="editorial" id="how-to-read"><p class="section-label">HOW TO READ ORBIT RESOURCES</p><div class="guide-note guide-links"><a href="#resource-index"><strong>Guide</strong><span>Read semantics and relationships.</span></a><a href="#reference-table"><strong>JSON Schema</strong><span>Inspect machine-valid structure.</span></a><a href="#resource-index"><strong>Invariants</strong><span>Check lifecycle meaning on each resource guide.</span></a><a href="#complete-example"><strong>Examples</strong><span>Follow a conforming resource.</span></a></div><p class="meta">JSON Schema validates structural conformance. ORBIT conformance may also depend on semantic invariants defined by the specification.</p></section>
</section></Layout>
